High-performance polyimide film is an advanced polymer material known for its exceptional thermal stability, electrical insulation, mechanical strength and chemical resistance. Its ability to perform across extreme temperatures makes it valuable in applications where conventional polymer films may not provide sufficient reliability.

Demand is increasing as manufacturers develop smaller, lighter and more sophisticated electronic devices. Flexible printed circuits, semiconductor components, high-frequency communication equipment and electric vehicle power systems require materials that maintain their electrical and mechanical properties under demanding operating conditions. Aerospace and defense applications further support demand for high-performance films capable of withstanding heat, vibration and harsh environments.

